        "original_id": "443d493a-4ea7-5a57-b551-fca435a4f32c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Fantin, William Kidd, Robert Culliford\n- Roles: sailor, pirate captain\n- Places: Indian Ocean\n- Topics: ship theft, piracy trial, execution\n\nFacts:\n- William Kidd, also known as Captain William Kidd or Captain Kidd, was a Scottish sailor born around 1654.\n- Jean Fantin is best known for having his ship stolen by William Kidd and Robert Culliford.\n- William Kidd returned from a voyage to the Indian Ocean.\n- William Kidd was tried for piracy after returning from the Indian Ocean voyage.\n- William Kidd was executed on 23 May 1701.",
